{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_y2anvpnk7u6r5onklprpw7nc7qlozxi66iuqnwo6ldvr6fn3elna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 12 tests pass in both dev and release mode, well within the 60-second timeout (8.14s in dev, 1.48s in release).\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C SparseHash implementation to safe, idiomatic Rust. Key implementation choices:\n\n**Sparse Array (`SparseArrayGroup.group: Vec<u8>`)**\n- Each occupied slot is stored as `[8 bytes LE size][size bytes data]` packed sequentially.\n- `position_to_offset` uses `u32::count_ones()` as the popcount.\n- Insertion uses `Vec::splice` to grow/replace, mirroring the C `realloc` + `memmove` pattern.\n- `is_position_occupied` and `set_position` mirror the C bitmap helpers.\n\n**Sparse Dictionary**\n- A bucket is serialized as `[klen | vlen | hash | key bytes | value bytes]` (24-byte header) inside the underlying SparseArray.\n- Lookup uses FNV-1a hashing + quadratic probing exactly like the C version: `(hash + n*n) & (max - 1)`.\n- On set: probe to find an empty slot or matching key. Replacing same-key skips the resize check; new insertions trigger `rehash_and_grow` once `bucket_count/bucket_max >= 80%`.\n- `rehash_and_grow` doubles `bucket_max`, rebuilds a fresh array, and copies each occupied bucket using its stored hash.\n- Used `bucket_data.to_vec()` snapshots to satisfy Rust's borrow checker without `unsafe`.\n\n**No `unsafe`, no FFI** — everything is pure safe Rust using `Vec<u8>`, slicing, and `from_le_bytes`/`to_le_bytes`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":47767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70485a69-ec24-41f3-ba43-79641a7d52ef","uuid":"1ef16688-e584-40c5-a0